# Port and Env Contracts

## Fixed ports — no fallback

| Surface | Port | Source of truth |
|---|---|---|
| React (delivery-ops client) | `8899` | `apps/delivery-ops/client/package.json` `PORT=8899` (`start` script) |
| Express (delivery-ops server) | `8001` | `apps/delivery-ops/server/.env` `PORT=8001`, fallback `8001` in `server/index.js:25` |

**No fallback / no auto-detect.** React is `8899`, Express is `8001`. Do not reintroduce `8888` or probe for a free port. This is per `AGENTS.md` Project defaults: fixed ports, no fallback; stale `8888` conflicts on shared hosts.

- `client/package.json:proxy` → `http://localhost:8001` (dev-only, CRA proxy).
- `server/index.js:25` → `PORT=8001` default (not `8888`).
- `apps/bin-packing/` is static-mounted under the same Express server — no extra port.

## Env contract — AI key is NAI, no fallback

| Key | Value | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `NAI_API_KEY` | canonical — **no `AI_API_KEY` fallback** | `apps/delivery-ops/server/.env` from `tokens.corp.nutanix.com` |

Files that must stay in sync on key name (per `ai-config-sync-nai-vs-ai-key.md` memory):

- `shared/src/connectors/aiConnector.ts` — reads `NAI_API_KEY` only (canonical source)
- `apps/delivery-ops/server/.env.example` — documents `NAI_API_KEY`
- `apps/delivery-ops/server/config/aiConfig.json` — `description` field names `NAI_API_KEY`
- `apps/delivery-ops/server/services/naiService.js` — error re-throw wording says `NAI_API_KEY`
- Lighthouse worktree mirrors: `lighthouse/app/server/config/aiConfig.json`, `lighthouse/app/server/.env.example` (if present)

**No fallback.** Per 2026-11-18 decision: `NAI_API_KEY` is the only name. Do not read `AI_API_KEY` as alias — `aiConnector.ts` reads `NAI_API_KEY` only. Adding a fallback reintroduces desync (see `never-hide-fix-root-cause-first.md`).

